    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d279">

                <pb facs="0438" n="350" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg350"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Baron Fava to Mr.
                            Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Italy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington, D.
                                C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1892-07-21"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 21, 1892</hi></date>. (Received July
                        21.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Foster</hi>: I notified by cable to his
                    excellency the minister of foreign affairs the contents of yours of the 18th
                    instant, and also the note of the Acting Secretary of the Navy.</p>
                <p>In answer, his excellency cablegrams as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Willingly accepting courteous invitation I now order that the royal
                            cruiser ‘<hi rendition="#italic">Bausan</hi>’ be at New York in the
                            beginning of October.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>I desire to assure you, and, through you, the Hon. Mr. Soley, of the intense
                    pleasure I feel in making you this communication.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fava.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
